<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-18> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Law 18: Rosas, Mediano & Rajpal (2024) O-Information & Higher-Order Synergy Decomposition Law" ;
    dct:description "Quantifies higher-order synergistic information in biological collectives where the whole carries information absent from any part | Variables: H(X^n): joint Shannon entropy; H(X^n_{-i}): leave-one-out entropy; Ω(X^n): O-information (redundancy minus synergy)" ;
    dct:source "Rosas & Rajpal (2024) @drmichaellevin [dar1gG3lWoc]; Pigozzi et al. (2025) [RLsPP8EfRDg]" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L149-L153>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L277-L289> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def o_information_3var (h_joint h1 h2 h3 h_m1 h_m2 h_m3 : Int) : Int :=
  (3 - 2) * h_joint + ((h1 - h_m1) + (h2 - h_m2) + (h3 - h_m3))
theorem rosas_rajpal_oinformation_synergy_xor_law :
    o_information_3var 2 1 1 1 2 2 2 = -1 ∧
    o_information_3var 1 1 1 1 1 1 1 = 1 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Ω(X^n) = (n - 2) H(X^n) + ∑_{i=1}^n [H(X_i) - H(X^n_{-i})];   Ω(XOR_3) = -1 bit < 0 (synergy)  vs.  Ω(COPY_3) = +1 bit > 0 (redundancy)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1966.10502008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0425>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/biomimetics8010110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25050748>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e26040288>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24010285> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Complete 25-Law Mathematical Atlas of Multiscale Bioelectricity, Low-Rattling, Epiplexity, Polycomputing, Natural Induction, Active Inference, Causal Emergence & Multicellular Evolution" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.o_information_3var" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.rosas_rajpal_oinformation_synergy_xor_law" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-19> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Law 19: John C. Doyle (2025) Bode Sensitivity Integral ('Waterbed Effect') & Layered Control Architecture Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves why robust biological feedback control requires layered slow-fast (bow-tie) architectures to manage conserved sensitivity tradeoffs | Variables: S(iω) = 1/(1 + L(iω)): closed-loop sensitivity function; S_low: disturbance attenuation band; S_high: out-of-band fragility amplification" ;
    dct:source "Doyle (2025) @drmichaellevin [Equ3sChCuqI]; Kearney, Shames, Schouten, Egré & Evans (2026) [m96j6MXcisw]" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L155-L159>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L291-L303> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def bode_high_band_amplification (total_integral s_low : Int) : Int :=
  total_integral - s_low
theorem doyle_bode_sensitivity_integral_waterbed_conservation (k : Int) :
    bode_high_band_amplification 0 (-k) = k ∧
    (-k) + bode_high_band_amplification 0 (-k) = 0 := by
  simp [bode_high_band_amplification]; omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "∫_0^∞ ln|S(iω)| dω = 0   (S_low + S_high = 0 ⟹ S_low = -k < 0 forces fragility peak S_high = +k > 0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1966.10502008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0425>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/biomimetics8010110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25050748>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e26040288>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24010285> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Complete 25-Law Mathematical Atlas of Multiscale Bioelectricity, Low-Rattling, Epiplexity, Polycomputing, Natural Induction, Active Inference, Causal Emergence & Multicellular Evolution" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.bode_high_band_amplification" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.doyle_bode_sensitivity_integral_waterbed_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Law 2: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021, 2025) Voltage-Gated Gap-Junction Bistability & Wound Isolation Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs bioelectric domain bistability, automatic electrical isolation of depolarized wound/tumor regions, and 1H1T vs. 2H0T memory | Variables: V_i: cell transmembrane voltage; G_{ij}: symmetric voltage-gated innexin/connexin conductance; V_th: gating threshold" ;
    dct:source "Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) Bioelectrochemistry; @drmichaellevin [PIrHLnmI_9o], [-dJSvsP4fzo], [ZCNi05m1Fmg]" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L55-L59>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L33-L47> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gj_bell_denom (b_i b_j : Nat) : Nat := (1 + b_i) * (1 + b_j)
theorem cervera_levin_mafe_gap_junction_wound_isolation (b_i b_j : Nat) :
    gj_bell_denom b_i b_j = gj_bell_denom b_j b_i ∧
    gj_bell_denom 0 0 = 1 ∧ gj_bell_denom 148 148 = 22201 := by
  refine ⟨?_, by decide, by decide⟩; simp [gj_bell_denom, Nat.mul_comm]
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "C_m dV_i/dt = -I_dep(V_i) - I_hyp(V_i) + ∑_j G_{ij}(V_i, V_j)(V_j - V_i),   G_{ij} = G_0 / [(1 + exp((V_i - V_th)/V_0))(1 + exp((V_j - V_th)/V_0))]" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1966.10502008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0425>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/biomimetics8010110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25050748>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e26040288>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24010285> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Complete 25-Law Mathematical Atlas of Multiscale Bioelectricity, Low-Rattling, Epiplexity, Polycomputing, Natural Induction, Active Inference, Causal Emergence & Multicellular Evolution" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.gj_bell_denom" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.cervera_levin_mafe_gap_junction_wound_isolation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-20> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Law 20: Shreesha, Morozov & Levin (2025, 2026) Spatialized Multicellular Prisoner's Dilemma Merge/Split Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves why single-cell cooperators fail (π_C(1) = -1 < 0) while agent-controlled boundary merging stabilizes multicellularity at k ≥ 4 and dominates defectors at k > 16 | Variables: k: multicellular cooperator cluster size; f_int(k) = 1 - 1/√k: internal cooperator interface fraction; b, c: benefit and cost" ;
    dct:source "Shreesha & Levin (2025) OSF kpzju_v2 & @drmichaellevin [iOFHyNliS9M]; Morozov (2026) [oe6v2fTewyU]; Le [Q-yZ-IeZywg]" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L161-L165>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L309-L322> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def multicell_coop_scaled_payoff (sqrt_k b c : Int) : Int :=
  (sqrt_k - 1) * b - sqrt_k * c
def multicell_defect_scaled_payoff (b : Int) : Int := b
theorem shreesha_morozov_multicellular_prisoners_dilemma_threshold :
    multicell_coop_scaled_payoff 1 2 1 = -1 ∧
    multicell_coop_scaled_payoff 2 2 1 = 0 ∧
    multicell_coop_scaled_payoff 4 2 1 = multicell_defect_scaled_payoff 2 ∧
    multicell_coop_scaled_payoff 6 2 1 > multicell_defect_scaled_payoff 2 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "π_C(k) = (1 - 1/√k) b - c ≥ 0 ⟺ √k ≥ b / (b - c);   π_C(k) > π_D(k) = b/√k ⟺ √k > 2b / (b - c)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1966.10502008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0425>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/biomimetics8010110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25050748>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e26040288>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24010285> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Complete 25-Law Mathematical Atlas of Multiscale Bioelectricity, Low-Rattling, Epiplexity, Polycomputing, Natural Induction, Active Inference, Causal Emergence & Multicellular Evolution" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.multicell_coop_scaled_payoff" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.shreesha_morozov_multicellular_prisoners_dilemma_threshold" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-21> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Law 21: Vitaly Vanchurin (2026) Geometric Framework for Biological Evolution & Fisher-Riemannian Gradient Law" ;
    dct:description "Unifies evolutionary natural selection and neural learning as Riemannian natural-gradient ascent on a statistical manifold | Variables: θ^i: trainable developmental/genetic coordinates; g_{ij}(θ): Fisher information metric tensor; U(θ): evolutionary fitness potential" ;
    dct:source "Vanchurin (2026) @drmichaellevin [3_XRPv1OcPg]; Levin (2026) [ur-zHu1TOOI]" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L167-L171>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L324-L335> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def fisher_fitness_rate (g11 g22 du1 du2 : Nat) : Nat :=
  g11 * du1 * du1 + g22 * du2 * du2
theorem vanchurin_geometric_evolution_fisher_natural_gradient_pos :
    fisher_fitness_rate 2 2 3 0 = 18 ∧
