<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Law 6: Finzi, Kolter & Wilson (2026) Epiplexity Decomposition (Bounded-Observer Structural Information Law)" ;
    dct:description "Resolves why deterministic sorting/CA trajectories have zero conditional Shannon entropy given the seed yet high observer-relative Epiplexity | Variables: L_F(X): prequential MDL code length; E_F(X): structural epiplexity; H_F(X): time-bounded residual entropy" ;
    dct:source "Finzi, Qiu, Jiang, Izmailov, Kolter & Wilson (2026) @drmichaellevin [_U8AwUq_aJQ]; Ruffini [b0wxfjpxB60]; Giorgini [P75iVMmbqQk]" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L78-L81>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L97-L111> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def epiplexity_total_code (epiplexity residual_entropy : Nat) : Nat :=
  epiplexity + residual_entropy
theorem finzi_wilson_epiplexity_decomposition (epiplexity residual_entropy : Nat) :
    epiplexity_total_code epiplexity residual_entropy - residual_entropy = epiplexity ∧
    epiplexity_total_code 82 12 = 94 ∧ epiplexity_total_code 82 0 = 82
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L_F(X) = E_F(X) + H_F(X)   (H_true(X | seed) = 0 ∧ E_F(X) > 0 for computationally bounded observer class F)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1966.10502008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0425>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/biomimetics8010110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25050748>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e26040288>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24010285> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Complete 25-Law Mathematical Atlas of Multiscale Bioelectricity, Low-Rattling, Epiplexity, Polycomputing, Natural Induction, Active Inference, Causal Emergence & Multicellular Evolution" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.epiplexity_total_code" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.finzi_wilson_epiplexity_decomposition" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-7> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Law 7: Tom Froese (2024, 2025) Irruption Theory & Euler 1/e Optimal-Stopping Law" ;
    dct:description "Quantifies the dimensionless 1/e exploration-to-commitment phase transition in physiological and agency dynamics | Variables: N: candidate horizon; k^*: optimal sample-to-commitment switch step; 1/e ≈ 0.3679: Euler dimensionless stopping constant" ;
    dct:source "Froese (2024) Entropy 26(4):288; @drmichaellevin [XA3DCTtRpDU], [F-pmWY4c4Dk]" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L83-L88>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L113-L122> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def froese_stopping_bracket (k e_scaled N_scaled : Nat) : Bool :=
  decide (k * e_scaled ≤ N_scaled ∧ N_scaled < (k + 1) * e_scaled)
theorem froese_irruption_euler_optimal_stopping_law :
    froese_stopping_bracket 37 2718 100566 = true := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_opt(N, k^*) = (k^*/N) ∑_{j=k^*}^{N-1} (1/j) → 1/e ≈ 0.367879   at   k^* = ⌊N/e⌋  (37/100 for N=100)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1966.10502008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0425>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/biomimetics8010110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25050748>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e26040288>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24010285> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Complete 25-Law Mathematical Atlas of Multiscale Bioelectricity, Low-Rattling, Epiplexity, Polycomputing, Natural Induction, Active Inference, Causal Emergence & Multicellular Evolution" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.froese_stopping_bracket" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.froese_irruption_euler_optimal_stopping_law" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-8> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Law 8: Bongard & Levin (2023) Polycomputing & Stoica (2024) Multi-Observer Commutative Readout Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves how one physical trajectory simultaneously computes XOR, AND, and OR (and dual S_6 sorting observables) under distinct observer lenses | Variables: F: single physical substrate dynamics; π_m: m-th observer coarse-graining projection" ;
    dct:source "Bongard & Levin (2023) Biomimetics 8(1):110; @drmichaellevin [9aTqeCzdT_c], [-0YvVQNMFFg], [qxrGa8ThLLo], [1dTRe2mOEfQ]" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L90-L95>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L128-L144> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def poly_state (a b : Bool) : Nat := a.toNat + b.toNat
def poly_obs_xor (s : Nat) : Bool := s % 2 == 1
def poly_obs_and (s : Nat) : Bool := decide (s ≥ 2)
def poly_obs_or  (s : Nat) : Bool := decide (s ≥ 1)
theorem bongard_levin_polycomputing_dual_observer_exact (a b : Bool) :
    poly_obs_xor (poly_state a b) = bne a b ∧
    poly_obs_and (poly_state a b) = (a && b) ∧
    poly_obs_or  (poly_state a b) = (a || b) := by cases a <;> cases b <;> decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "x_{t+1} = F(x_t),   y^{(m)}_t = π_m(x_t) = g_m(a, b)   (π_1 = XOR, π_2 = AND, π_3 = OR;   π_I(v) = I(v) vs. π_E(v) = E(v) on S_n)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1966.10502008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0425>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/biomimetics8010110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25050748>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e26040288>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24010285> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Complete 25-Law Mathematical Atlas of Multiscale Bioelectricity, Low-Rattling, Epiplexity, Polycomputing, Natural Induction, Active Inference, Causal Emergence & Multicellular Evolution" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.poly_state" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.bongard_levin_polycomputing_dual_observer_exact" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/levin-youtube-channel-math-9> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Law 9: Ziming Liu (2024) Kolmogorov-Arnold Network (KAN) Univariate Spline Superposition Law" ;
    dct:description "Replaces fixed-activation linear weights with learnable 1D edge splines to discover symbolic laws of biological dynamics | Variables: n: input state dimension; φ_{q,p}: learnable 1D inner spline functions; Φ_q: 2n+1 outer univariate functions" ;
    dct:source "Liu et al. (2024) KAN & @drmichaellevin [uupyXjSnZiA]; Kumar [1mXUFweWOug]" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L97-L100>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/bfe377c2/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean#L146-L159> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def kan_outer_summands (n : Nat) : Nat := 2 * n + 1
def kan_inner_edges (n : Nat) : Nat := n * (2 * n + 1)
theorem liu_kolmogorov_arnold_network_superposition_law (n : Nat) :
    kan_outer_summands 4 = 9 ∧ kan_inner_edges 4 = 36 ∧
    kan_outer_summands (n + 1) - kan_outer_summands n = 2
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "f(x_1, …, x_n) = ∑_{q=0}^{2n} Φ_q( ∑_{p=1}^n φ_{q,p}(x_p) ),   N_outer(n) = 2n + 1,   N_edges(n) = n(2n + 1)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tree.2015.11.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-025-08411-2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/01621459.1966.10502008>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2017.0425>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abc6182>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2019.02688>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/biomimetics8010110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e25050748>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/e26040288>,
        <https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24010285> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Complete 25-Law Mathematical Atlas of Multiscale Bioelectricity, Low-Rattling, Epiplexity, Polycomputing, Natural Induction, Active Inference, Causal Emergence & Multicellular Evolution" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.kan_outer_summands" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "LoopLevinYouTubeChannelMath.liu_kolmogorov_arnold_network_superposition_law" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "MorphoEval simulation-faithfulness rubric v0.1.0" ;
    dct:description "Weighted 0-100 rubric for the faithfulness of a morphology simulation to its organism and source model; Overall = weighted mean. Each score is a pk:LLMClaimAssessment (Project Delphi rubric-assessment template) of the pk:Claim pkr:claim/morphoeval-<sim> against one dimension (dct:subject the dimension concept, pk:assessmentType morphoeval/<version>/<dimension>) with pk:hasScore = score/100 — an uncalibrated rubric score, not a probability — and a pk:hasVerdict band; the overall score has the rubric itself as dct:subject and is also the pk:weightOfEvidence of the claim." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/rubric.yaml> ;
    skos:narrower <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity>,
